"learning.card.yoga.section1.title" = "Types of anti-stress yoga";
"learning.card.yoga.section1.content" = "Yoga is much more than a physical practice. It's a powerful stress regulation tool that acts on your body AND your mind.\n\n• Hatha Yoga: gentle, perfect for beginners\n• Yin Yoga: long postures, very relaxing\n• Yoga Nidra: guided lying meditation\n• Vinyasa: dynamic but meditative";
"learning.card.yoga.section2.title" = "Effects on cortisol";
"learning.card.yoga.section2.content" = "• Many people feel calmer after a single session\n• Effects build up with regular practice\n• Studies associate regular yoga with lower stress";
"learning.card.yoga.section3.title" = "Scientifically proven benefits";
"learning.card.yoga.section3.content" = "Physical:\n• Flexibility and muscle strength\n• Better posture\n• May ease chronic pain\n• Improved balance\n\nMental:\n• May reduce anxiety symptoms\n• Better emotional regulation\n• Improved concentration\n\nPhysiological:\n• Activation of the parasympathetic system (relaxation)\n• Better heart rate variability\n• May support digestion";
"learning.card.yoga.section4.title" = "What happens in your brain";
"learning.card.yoga.section4.content" = "• Increased GABA (calming neurotransmitter)\n• Reduced amygdala activity (fear/stress)\n• Activated prefrontal cortex (emotional control)";
"learning.card.yoga.section5.title" = "No need to be flexible";
"learning.card.yoga.section5.content" = "Yoga isn't a competition. Every body is different, and the anti-stress benefits come from the very first sessions, even with adaptations!";

